<TrustPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Havemoon handles browser-tool entries, technical logs, analytics, advertising data, cookies, contact messages, and privacy choices."
  updated="August 14, 2026"
>
  <h2>Publisher and scope</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon operates this English-language knowledge base at
    <a href="https://sohotation.xyz/">sohotation.xyz</a>. This policy covers the site's guides,
    resources, browser tools, search, and messages sent to its published contact address. Havemoon
    does not offer user accounts or ask visitors to create a profile on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Information processed in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The calculators and checklists process entries in your browser for the current page session.
    They do not submit those values to Havemoon. Avoid entering confidential supplier, payment,
    personal, or regulated data.
  </p>

  <h2>Local storage</h2>
  <p>
    The site stores a theme preference in the browser so that light or dark mode remains consistent.
    Search runs against an index of the site's public content. These functions do not require a user
    account.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare is used to deliver and protect the site. Cloudflare and the site's hosting
    infrastructure may process ordinary request and security information such as an IP address, user
    agent, requested URL, referring page, response status, time, and security events. These records
    are used to deliver pages, prevent abuse, diagnose faults, and maintain security. Retention is
    limited by the relevant service settings and operational need.
  </p>

  <h2>Messages sent to Havemoon</h2>
  <p>
    If you email Havemoon, the message, sender address, headers, and any information you choose to
    include are processed to answer the request, keep an appropriate record, and protect the service
    from abuse. Do not send supplier bank details, identity documents, product secrets, or other
    sensitive files unless a secure method has been agreed. Messages are retained only as long as
    reasonably needed for the inquiry, legal obligations, dispute handling, or security.
  </p>

  <h2>Website analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon uses Google Analytics 4 to understand page views, navigation, referring pages, browser
    and device categories, approximate location, and site performance. Google may process cookie or
    device identifiers and interaction events for this measurement. Havemoon does not intentionally
    send entries from its browser tools, email messages, supplier records, or other sensitive
    information to Analytics. Where consent is required, analytics storage follows the choices
    presented through the site's Google-certified consent message.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising, consent, and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon may use Google AdSense to display and measure advertising. Ads may not appear on every
    page or during account review. Google and third-party vendors may use cookies, web beacons, IP
    addresses, or similar identifiers to serve and measure ads. Third-party vendors, including
    Google, use advertising cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this site or
    other sites. Users can review or change personalized advertising choices in
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a> or
    use the
    <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">About Ads opt-out page</a
    >. Google also publishes information about
    <a href="https://support.google.com/admanager/answer/9012903" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
      >advertising technology providers</a
    > and available controls.
  </p>

  <h2>Consent choices</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon does not request personalized advertising where applicable consent is required unless
    an appropriate consent mechanism is active. Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United
    Kingdom, or Switzerland may receive a Google-certified consent message before advertising
    storage or personalized advertising is used. The message provides the available accept, reject,
    manage, and withdrawal choices. Browser settings may also be used to block or delete cookies,
    although this can affect site or advertising features.
  </p>

  <h2>Google data-use information</h2>
  <p>
    For an explanation of how Google uses data when a visitor uses a partner site or app, see
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
      >How Google uses data when you use our partners' sites or apps</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    Guides link to regulators and other primary sources. External websites operate under their own
    privacy policies; Havemoon does not control their collection practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is written for business buyers and import professionals and is not directed to
    children under 13. Havemoon does not knowingly ask children to provide personal information
    through this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on applicable law, you may ask about access, correction, deletion, restriction, or
    objection concerning information supplied directly to Havemoon. A request may require reasonable
    verification and may be limited where retention is required by law, security, or legitimate
    recordkeeping needs.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact and data requests</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon is the publisher and site operator. Privacy questions and data requests can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:contact@havemoon.com">contact@havemoon.com</a>. Include enough information to
    identify the request, but do not send passwords, government identification, bank details, or
    unrelated confidential documents.
  </p>
</TrustPage>
